### self-test on the run box
  PASS the limit rides WITH the verdict: the body-checked read is declared un-run, beside the green
lane_identity SELF-TEST: OK

### the LANE's current cfg — digest only, and it is NOT a check
DIGEST <DIGEST-A: the lane's current cfg>
⛔ THIS IS NOT A CHECK. It reports what the dir authenticates as, so a human who knows the
   intended account can record it as --expect. Comparing this to itself blesses whatever is there.
rc=0

### the dir HC1 fired under, for contrast — do they differ?
DIGEST <DIGEST-B: the cfg HC1 fired under>

### and the REFUSAL that matters: no expectation supplied
REFUSE rc 4: no --expect supplied. A MISSING EXPECTATION IS NOT A PASS — that is the same defect this tool exists to fix, one level up. Use --print-digest to obtain a value to record.
rc=0

########## exit codes read from the COMMAND, not from a pipe ##########
### the refusal arm, exit code read from the COMMAND and not from a pipe
REFUSE rc 4: no --expect supplied. A MISSING EXPECTATION IS NOT A PASS — that is the same defect this tool exists to fix, one level up. Use --print-digest to obtain a value to record.
TRUE rc=4   (a pipe into head read 0 for this same command)

### and a MISMATCH against a deliberately wrong expectation, same rule
REFUSE rc 5: IDENTITY MISMATCH. expected 0000000000000000 · got <DIGEST-A: the lane's current cfg>
   (neither account is named: only digests cross this boundary, per the infra-name gate)
TRUE rc=5

### and the credential half, offline, against the lane's own digest
IDENTITY OK: the config dir authenticates as the expected account (digest <DIGEST-A: the lane's current cfg>).
    credential: present · refresh token present · access token valid
    ⛔ THIS IS THE OFFLINE SHAPE ONLY. §Q3.4 item 2's trivial AUTHENTICATED READ, checked by its
       BODY, is NOT performed here and is still owed at the preflight.
TRUE rc=0
